ality reasons let's not look  into them right now but let's rather  focus on the other side of my profession  and as all of you know watching this  channel i also do have this youtube  channel firm learning for those of you  who see this the first time i'm a former  mckinsey consultant and on my channel i  talk about how to be successful in the  first years of your career i talk about  slight writing tips excel advice other  career related topics consulting  weighted topics so like and subscribe if  this is something that you're interested  in and how the okr system is set up is  that you always start with an objective  so here for instance in the first line  youtube to become the leading career and  consulting creator on youtube but then  you always have the key results so you  measure this objective by achieving  these key results which should be  objective and measurable in the end so  here for instance how many youtube  videos i want to create each week so i  want to continue to create one quality  youtube video every single week and then  i also want to do a couple of additional  things so to ideate and launch a new  content format for youtube so stay tuned  on what that is going to be a trust you  will learn about it soon over the course  of the year if you want to learn more  about what these okrs are all about how  these work i created another video last  year about exactly this topic i will  link it somewhere above here so that i  don't need to repeat myself but you can  just look it up if you're interested in  it by the way if you do like this excel  sheet that are prepared to track the  goals i will offer it for you as a  download of course for free just check  the video description for the download  link and you will get it sent to your  personal inbox overall if i do compare  these goals to the goals that i said a  year ago especially these numeric ones  on subscriber growth i must say that are  significantly underdelivered on some of  them but on the o