at  opportunities that open up only due to  this that i would never even have  dreamed of when i started all of this in  early 2020 so think about what could be  other projects that you would be open  and willing to do on top of your regular  nine to 5 job if you do find the time  for that and can commit to consistently  deliver on such a project my experience  is that good things will likely come to  you next are my goals in the health and  sports section so even number one for me  is to get back into the running shape  this is one of the areas where i did  significantly under deliver last year i  wanted to run a marathon then the  marathon was cancelled due to the health  situation and this pretty much took away  all the motivation for me to really  engage in a regular running practice  this is what i now want to re-engage in  this year get back into a regular  running practice and then potentially  include three also run a marathon once  again and then the next point is signing  up for a gym so one of the perks of  working at building raider is the  directly next to the office there's a  really high quality gym that almost all  employees attend and is very well  accepted to hit the gym for an hour or  so every single day so i do want to take  advantage of that sign up for the gym  and probably establish a habit of two or  three times per week going to the gym  hitting the gym and getting some  additional training in this way last but  not least my personal growth goals so  even though this is something i did  wanted to complete in the last year i  did not complete my phd yet so one of  these other things where i did not have  the progress that i wanted to have but  this year hopefully will be the year i  did make some significant progress last  year i have now the key paper of my phd  under review with a pretty awesome  journal so let's see whether this goes  through that would be pretty amazing i  will let you know once this is decided  so making some significan